The first is the order. If the user types the pattern before the text, the program asks for the text and then reads the pattern as the first line of it. If the text is never finished, because nobody types the blank line, the pattern waits for it, and the user is left staring at a prompt. The fix is to read the pattern first, before anything else, and check it before a single line of text is read. Read that way the text can come in any order. And the prompt only checks that the pattern compiles. It never asks about the text, and the text is the part nobody checks.

